title: Design for Disassembly
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The cushions on the [[Oka Chair]] come off with toggles. The frame is held with bolts. Anyone with a wrench can take the whole chair apart.

That is the idea: decide how a thing comes apart while you are deciding how it goes together. Bolts over glue. Parts that can be told apart.

It is what lets a worn part be replaced, and what lets each material go back where it belongs at the end. Without it you get a [[Monstrous Hybrid]].

See [[Technical Nutrient]], [[Biological Nutrient]], [[Catifa Carta]], [[adaptive reuse]], [[Cradle to Cradle]]
